CLAUDE.md

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Full JSC test set (~166k samples) for Gate 1b. Tens of MB, fully regenerable by re-running
# training/dwn_jsc_kaggle.ipynb, and only the host script consumes it. The 1000-sample
# _testvectors.npz IS committed -- the RTL testbenches depend on it.
training/artifacts/*_testset_full.npz

# Phase 2 sweep checkpoints. NOT a preference -- a hard constraint:
#   * projected ~933 MB across the 32-config grid
#   * the largest single file (n6_z800_distributive_w360) is ~122 MB, above GitHub's 100 MB
#     per-file limit, so the push would be REJECTED outright
# The size is LearnableMapping: it stores a [nodes x n x input_bits] weight tensor, ~423 bytes
# per node-per-z, and z is a sweep axis.
#
# These are NOT cheaply regenerable -- training needs a Kaggle GPU because torch_dwn has no CPU
# path -- so treat them like the 166k test set: they do not travel with a clone, and a machine
# that wants to re-run the sweep must re-train (training/train_grid_kaggle.ipynb) or copy them
# across. Phase 1's artifacts stay committed and stay where they are; verify_phase1.py,
# host.py, run_tb.py and run_gate1.py all locate those by hardcoded path.
training/artifacts/sweeps/

# Generated build products (Vivado reports, netlists, bitstreams).
# Everything under build/ is regenerable by re-running the flow that made it.
build/

# Vivado scratch and per-run droppings
.Xil/
*.jou
*.log
*.str
clockInfo.txt
*.backup.jou
*.backup.log
vivado_pid*.str
usage_statistics_webtalk.*
dfx_runtime.txt
.cache/
hs_err_pid*.log

# Vivado project mode (we use the non-project batch flow, but IP or GUI runs leave these)
*.cache/
*.hw/
*.ip_user_files/
*.runs/
*.sim/
*.xpr

# conifer scratch. conifer's FixedPointConverter writes a pybind11 helper into
# `./.fp_converter_<type>_<timestamp+random>/` relative to the CURRENT WORKING DIRECTORY, so it
# lands in the repo root rather than under build/. The suffix is regenerated per construction,
# so these accumulate rather than being reused. Only the VHDL backend builds one -- and that
# backend does not work on Windows anyway (it shells out to `g++ ... -o X.so`) -- but the
# directory is left behind even when the compile fails, which is how the first one appeared.
.fp_converter_*/
